{
  "_comment": "Central UI string source for every finlink client (clients/android, clients/switch, clients/3ds, clients/nds, clients/web) -- single source of truth so the same concept reads identically everywhere instead of drifting per platform. Generated per-client resource files (see generate.py) are committed, same pattern as clients/web/finlink_core.js: a normal build never needs to run generate.py, only a change to this file does. Placeholders are {0}, {1}, ... in argument order; 'placeholders' (only present when a string has any) lists each one's type ('s' = string, 'd' = integer) so generate.py can emit the right printf/Android format specifier. Every client auto-selects its language from the system language (falling back to 'en' when the system language can't be determined or has no translation here), with a manual override in Settings -- add another key per string here to support a further language later. A key missing a given language falls back to 'en' at generation time (see generate.py's own comment), so a new string can be added in English first and translated later without breaking any client.",

